+# Why CVE-2026-62292 Does Not Affect `libheif` 1.11.0 on Debian Bullseye
+
+## CVE-2026-62292 – Out-of-bounds Read in Uncompressed `unci` Tile Range Slicing
+
+- **Component:** `unc_decoder::get_compressed_image_data_uncompressed` / `unc_decoder::fetch_tile_data` (`libheif/codecs/uncompressed/unc_decoder.cc`)
+- **CWE:** CWE-125 (Out-of-bounds Read)
+- **Issue:** Tile range validation uses `range_start_offset + range_size`. For a crafted zlib-compressed `unci` image, that addition wraps in `uint64_t`, the bounds check is skipped, and `memcpy` is called with an invalid source pointer and a ~1 TiB length, crashing tile decode via `heif_image_handle_decode_image_tile()`.
+- **Fix Commit:** `089a809bf6bed1abae102d5e97b6bb8c4f53b515`
+- **Upstream Status:** Fixed in upstream `libheif` 1.23.1; advisory affected range is **>= 1.19.0, < 1.23.1**
+
+---
+
+## Why Debian Bullseye (`libheif` 1.11.0-1+deb11u2) Is NOT Affected
+
+The vulnerability is confined to the **uncompressed HEIF decoder** tile-slicing path (`unci` / `cmpC` zlib full-item compression under `libheif/codecs/uncompressed/`). That codec was introduced experimentally in upstream **libheif 1.16.0**; the advisory's affected range begins at **1.19.0**. Both are after Bullseye's 1.11.0 baseline.
+
+In v1.11.0:
+
+- There is no uncompressed codec, `unc_decoder`, `cmpC` property handling, or `heif_image_handle_decode_image_tile()` API
+- The wrapped `range_start_offset + range_size` check cannot be reached
+
+### Verification
+
+```bash
+grep -rn "get_compressed_image_data_uncompressed\|fetch_tile_data\|unc_decoder" libheif/  # empty
+ls libheif/codecs/uncompressed/unc_decoder.cc                                          # missing
+grep -rn "heif_image_handle_decode_image_tile" .                                       # empty
+```
+
+### Debian Bullseye Package Details
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| Package | libheif |
+| Version | 1.11.0-1+deb11u2 |
+| Distribution | Debian 11 (Bullseye) |
+| Upstream Version | 1.11.0 |
+| Status | **NOT AFFECTED** |
+| Justification | `vulnerable_code_not_present` |
+
+**Status: NOT_AFFECTED — No action needed.**
