+# Why CVE-2026-50142 Does Not Affect `libheif` 1.11.0 on Debian Bullseye
+
+## CVE-2026-50142 – Unbounded Heap Allocation in HEIF Sequence Parser
+
+- **Component:** `Box_stsz::parse()` and `Track::load()` (`libheif/sequences/seq_boxes.cc`, `libheif/sequences/track.cc`)
+- **CWE:** CWE-770 (Allocation Without Limits); secondary CWE-190 (Integer Overflow)
+- **Issue:** `max_sequence_frames` is enforced only in the variable-size `stsz` branch, so a crafted fixed-size sample table can request about 4.29 billion samples. A per-chunk range check also adds two `uint32_t` values that can wrap.
+- **Fix Commit:** `a6caa38f7a70d66dc9caec2a7bfe20935b32c622` (fix version 1.23.0)
+- **Advisory affected range:** **>= 1.19.0, <= 1.22.2** (GHSA-jvmp-j3cw-84mh)
