+# Why CVE-2026-48029 Does Not Affect `libheif` 1.11.0 on Debian Bullseye
+
+## CVE-2026-48029 – Heap OOB Read in Rotated Grid Tile Decode
+
+- **Component:** `ImageItem_Grid::decode_grid_tile` and `transform_requested_tile_position_to_original_tile_position` (`libheif/api/libheif/heif_tiling.cc`, `libheif/image-items/image_item.cc`)
+- **CWE:** CWE-125 (Out-of-bounds Read); secondary CWE-191 (Integer Underflow)
+- **Issue:** A grid image with an `irot` of 90/180/270 and rows != columns underflows a `uint32_t` tile coordinate, and `decode_grid_tile` then indexes `m_grid_tile_ids` with `ty * cols + tx` without a bounds check.
+- **Fix Commit:** `e523ec0bf379110b7c33d4c159f8b1202d332157` (fix version 1.22.0)
+- **Advisory affected range:** **>= 1.19.0, < 1.22.0** (GHSA-6x5f-qchq-cxqv)
+
+---
+
+## Why Debian Bullseye (`libheif` 1.11.0-1+deb11u2) Is NOT Affected
+
+The vulnerable code was written after the 1.11.0 baseline, in a source layout that does not exist in 1.11.0. The grid decoder in 1.11.0 is `HeifContext::decode_full_grid_image` in `libheif/heif_context.cc`. It pastes each tile at a running offset (`x0 += src_width`) and never computes a tile index from a rotated coordinate, so the underflow cannot occur.
+
+In v1.11.0:
+
+- There is no `libheif/api/` or `libheif/image-items/` directory
+- There is no `transform_requested_tile_position_to_original_tile_position`, `ImageItem_Grid`, or `heif_image_handle_get_grid_image_tile_id`
+- Grid decoding has no `m_grid_tile_ids` lookup driven by rotated coordinates
+
+### Verification
+
+```bash
+grep -rn "transform_requested_tile_position_to_original_tile_position\|decode_grid_tile\|heif_image_handle_get_grid_image_tile_id\|ImageItem_Grid" libheif/  # empty
+ls libheif/api/libheif/heif_tiling.cc libheif/image-items/image_item.cc                                                                          # missing
+```
+
