Description: Fix CVE-2026-47247 heap information disclosure in grid image decoding
 HeifPixelImage::ImagePlane::alloc() used non-zero-initialising `new uint8_t[...]`,
 so padding regions (stride slack, rounded_size(), alignment slack) leaked
 uninitialised heap memory across decoded images.
 .
 In addition, the grid coverage check used integer division
 (`grid.get_width() / grid.get_columns()`), so undersized tiles could "cover"
 the canvas on paper while leaving gap columns/rows of uninitialised memory
 visible in the decoded output.
 .
 This patch:
   * switches ImagePlane allocation to `std::calloc()` (zero-initialised) and
     matches the destructor / free path accordingly, adding the required
     `<cstdlib>` include;
   * introduces a 64-bit-multiplication grid-coverage guard inside
     HeifContext::decode_full_grid_image so undersized tile grids are rejected
     with heif_suberror_Invalid_grid_data before any decoding occurs.
 .
 Backport of upstream commit 6aca89d76a5118bd47adcb5b83e7b01a32134985
 (released in v1.22.0) to Debian bullseye's libheif 1.11.0. The upstream file
 layout (libheif/image/pixelimage.cc, libheif/image-items/grid.cc) does not
 exist in 1.11.0; the equivalent code lives in libheif/heif_image.cc and
 libheif/heif_context.cc, so the hunks were re-anchored there. The upstream
 pixelimage.cc hunks in extend_padding_to_size() and extend_to_size_with_zero()
 have no counterpart in 1.11.0 (those functions do not exist yet) and are
 therefore omitted; only the destructor and ImagePlane::alloc() free/allocate
 sites needed conversion. The upstream grid.cc guard was rewritten against the
 v1.11.0 HeifContext::decode_full_grid_image tile loop (which previously had
 no coverage check at all -- the missing bytes were masked at paste time by
 std::min() clipping in decode_and_paste_tile_image, but the padding still
 leaked uninitialised memory).
 .
 Rebased onto the hooked tree: CVE-2026-32814 already added a memset() after
 the new[] at the ImagePlane allocation site. This patch replaces the new[] +
 memset() pair with a single std::calloc(), so the block is zero-filled once
 and std::free() in the destructor matches.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/strukturag/libheif/commit/6aca89d76a5118bd47adcb5b83e7b01a32134985
